# Review ownership.
#
# What this file does on its own: auto-request review from the listed owner when a pull
# request touches a matching path. That is all. It does NOT block a merge.
#
# Blocking requires a branch protection rule on main with "Require a pull request before
# merging" and "Require review from Code Owners" enabled — and, if the owner should not be
# able to merge past it themselves, "Do not allow bypassing the above settings". Without
# those, this file is a reminder, not a gate.
#
# Worth stating plainly because the failure is silent: an unenforced CODEOWNERS looks
# identical to an enforced one in the file listing, and reads as protection that is not there.
# It is also inert entirely on a private repo on the free plan.
#
# The paths below are the ones where review is the only real control, so the branch
# protection rule is not optional for them.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @PatMacalister

# The landing page is not open to contributions. It is published marketing copy for a tool
# whose credibility depends on not overclaiming, and its wording is deliberate — "never
# alarmist, never overclaim coverage, consequence language". Copy changes from outside are
# declined; see CONTRIBUTING.md. Bug reports about the page are welcome as issues.
/public/                @PatMacalister

# The egress allowlist and the module contract are the two places where review is the only
# real control. apiHosts is checked for shape, never for legitimacy: only a human can tell
# whether a hostname is genuinely the provider's API. Provider modules also execute at import,
# before validation, so the whole file has to be read — not just the diff.
/src/providers/         @PatMacalister
/src/core/resolve.mjs   @PatMacalister
/src/core/redact.mjs    @PatMacalister
